values ('ap_physics_c_em', 8, '8.1', array['8.1']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Electric permittivity', 'Electric permittivity is a measure of the degree to which a material or medium is polarized in the presence of an electric field; free space has a constant permittivity \epsilon_0, and matter''s permittivity differs from it because of the matter''s composition and arrangement.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-c-em-reference-u8-u10-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_c_em-u8-r2-004; ced=8.1.C.1: "Electric permittivity is a measurement of the degree to which a material or medium is polarized in the presence of an electric field."; 8.1.C.3; 8.1.C.4')
