values ('ap_physics_c_em', 8, '8.1', array['8.1']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Elementary charge and charges of particles', 'The elementary charge e is the magnitude of the charge of a single electron or proton and can be considered to be the smallest indivisible amount of charge; an electron has charge -e, a proton has charge +e, and a neutron has no electric charge.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-c-em-reference-u8-u10-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_c_em-u8-r3-001; ced=8.1.A.1.ii–iii: "The charge of an electron is −e and the charge of a proton is +e, and a neutron has no electric charge."; product-owner-directed correction by the Claude session (David, 2026-10-10): the escalated row was corrected against its own CED evidence and re-checked by both independent checkers and the own-family veto')
