values ('ap_physics_c_em', 8, '8.3', array['8.3']::text[], 'convention', 'Conductor in electrostatic equilibrium', 'In electrostatic equilibrium, the excess charge of a conductor lies on its surface, the electric field within the conductor is zero, and the field at the surface is perpendicular to the surface.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Zero field inside applies to a conductor in electrostatic equilibrium, not to insulators.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-c-em-reference-u8-u10-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_c_em-u8-r2-006; ced=8.3.B.1 and 8.3.B.1.i: "the excess charge of a conductor is distributed on the surface of the conductor, and the electric field within the conductor is zero"')
